 * `"main"`) to `NATIVE_ENTRY_VMAIN_SYMBOL`, then appends a tiny platform-ABI STUB `LFunc`, itself
 * named `"main"`, that receives the platform's own `argc`/`argv` entry registers, forwards them
 * to the runtime's `tk_set_args` BEFORE anything else runs, then calls the renamed virtual-main
 * and returns its result normalized to a platform-uniform exit code (`append_exit_status_mask`) —
 * mirroring the C emitter's own generated `main`
 * (`codegen.tks`'s `emit_program_main_body`: `int main(int argc, char **argv) { tk_set_args(argc,
